 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the TaskRepository's delete method filtering tasks by owner_id instead of task_id. The fix changes the query to delete only the task with the specified ID, ensuring only the target task is removed. This resolves the issue where deleting a task would delete all tasks of that owner.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/repository.py b/tracker/repository.py\nindex a9cc26b..8411052 100644\n--- a/tracker/repository.py\n+++ b/tracker/repository.py\n@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ class TaskRepository:\n \n     def delete(self, task_id):\n         with self.db.transaction() as conn:\n-            cur = conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM tasks WHERE owner_id = (SELECT owner_id FROM tasks WHERE id = ?)\", (task_id,))\n+            cur = conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM tasks WHERE id = ?\", (task_id,))\n             if cur.rowcount == 0:\n                 raise NotFoundError(f\"task {task_id} not found\")\n \n",
